Third-party code in src/port/sh
===============================

This folder is for SuperH from SH-2 on: SH-2, SH-2A, SH-3 and SH-4, in
either byte order.

The three files listed below come from NetBSD, copied byte for byte and
never edited. memcpy.S and memset.S carry the full text of their licence,
the three-clause BSD licence. memmove.S is three lines that define MEMMOVE
and include memcpy.S, with no notice of their own. The other files in this
folder belong to libterae and are under libterae's licence, given at the
top of each: port_memcpy.S, port_memmove.S and port_memset.S, which are the
files assembled, port_memcmp.c, and machine/asm.h, which stands in for
NetBSD's header of that name. No NetBSD header is used: NetBSD's
<machine/asm.h> for SuperH carries the University of California's licence
with its advertising clause.

The port_*.S files are checked by assembling them with GNU as, from
binutils built for sh-elf: see "What is checked" below.


